I'm entirely with guskant on this one.

On 07.04.2013 13:00, guskant wrote:
> OK, from yacc point of view, I agree with you. From a semantic point
> of view, however, FA KU should be an implicit expression of some
> possible sumti. In fact, for other sumtcita like BAI or tense, the
> usage of sumtcita means a vague expression (CLL9.9). Both modal-tense
> and FA are mod_head_490 of yacc. They should have the same semantic
> rule.

I agree. More than a year ago I suggested that {fi ku la .lojban. cu 
tavla} be the same as {fo la .lojban. cu tavla}.
Why? Because FA are sumtcita/TAG, and the rule for TAG is this:

TAG broda == TAG ku broda == TAG zo'e broda

(semantically, not grammatically)

Mentioning a FA but not filling it is much like filling it with zo'e 
explicitly, why else would you say {fi ku} in the first place?

mu'o mi'e la selpa'i

